# Privacy Policy

Effective date: July 4, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Workbooks ("Workbooks", "we", "us") collects, uses, shares, and
protects information when you use workbooks.sh, the Workbooks Cloud application, and related services
(the "Services"). Workbooks is operated by shinyobjectz, 968 NE Paula Drive, Bend, OR 97701, United
States. Questions: [shane@shinyobjectz.com](mailto:shane@shinyobjectz.com).

## Information we collect

- **Account information** — your name, email address, and authentication identifiers when you create
  an account or sign in.
- **Content you create** — the workbooks, documents, notes, and configuration you author or upload.
- **Connected-account data** — when you choose to connect a third-party account (for example Google,
  GitHub, Cloudflare, or Meta), we access only the data covered by the permissions you grant, solely
  to provide the features you asked for. This may include, from Meta Platforms (Facebook, Instagram,
  and WhatsApp Business), your Pages, ad accounts, advertising performance metrics, business assets,
  and content you authorize us to manage on your behalf.
- **Usage and device data** — log data, IP address, browser and device type, and interaction events,
  used to operate and secure the Services.

## How we use information

We use information to operate, maintain, and improve the Services; to authenticate you; to perform the
actions you request through connected accounts (such as creating or managing advertising campaigns and
publishing or measuring content on platforms you connect); to communicate with you; to provide support;
to detect and prevent fraud and abuse; and to comply with legal obligations.

We do not sell your personal information. We do not use data obtained from a connected platform for any
purpose other than providing and improving the features you enabled, consistent with that platform's
terms.

## How we share information

- **Service providers** — vendors who host, process, or support the Services under contract (for
  example our cloud and infrastructure providers), limited to what they need to perform their work.
- **Platforms you connect** — to perform an action you request, we transmit the necessary data to the
  connected platform (for example, sending a campaign definition to Meta's advertising API).
- **Legal and safety** — where required by law, or to protect the rights, safety, and security of our
  users, the public, or Workbooks.

We do not share connected-platform data with third parties for their own marketing.

## Data retention

We retain information for as long as your account is active or as needed to provide the Services, then
delete or de-identify it, except where a longer period is required by law. You may request deletion at
any time — see [[data-deletion]].

## Your choices and rights

You may access, correct, export, or delete your information, and disconnect any connected account at any
time from your account settings. Disconnecting revokes our access to that platform's data going forward.
Depending on your location, you may have additional rights under laws such as the GDPR or CCPA; contact
us to exercise them.

## Security

We use administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect information, including
encryption of credentials and connection tokens at rest. No method of transmission or storage is
perfectly secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.

## International users

Workbooks is operated from the United States. If you use the Services from outside the United States,
you consent to processing your information in the United States and other countries where we or our
providers operate.

## Children

The Services are not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age required in your jurisdiction),
and we do not knowingly collect their information.

## Changes

We may update this Policy. Material changes will be posted here with a new effective date, and where
appropriate we will notify you.

